                  <provenance type="#l"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_474">St Albans,
                        Hertfordshire. Benedictine abbey of St Alban</orgName><p> According to the
                        Gesta abbatum S. Albani, at the time of Abbot Geoffrey (1119–46) was
                        produced 'unum psalterium pretiosum totum similiter auro illuminatum'. The
                        description is thought to fit to this book, in which each psalm, canticle
                        and collect begins with an initial in burnished gold. </p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Bought for 2s. 6d. by Richard Heber
                     (1773–1833).</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">It was lot 1247 in the sale of Heber's
                     manuscripts by Mr Evans at 93 Pall Mall on 10 February 1836.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Thomas Phillipps</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">William Morris</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Mr Brian S. Cron, Kew (1913–2002). </provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Sold to the British Library in
                     2006.</provenance>
               </history>
